Five Letters word list
----------------------
The allowed-guess list in web/games/words.js is taken from Webster's New International Dictionary (1934),
which is in the public domain (as distributed in /usr/share/dict/words on macOS and BSD systems), plus plurals
formed from its four-letter words.


Flag Quiz flag images
---------------------
The country flags in web/games/flags/ (used by the Flag Quiz game) come from the flag-icons project
(https://github.com/lipis/flag-icons, 4x3 set), Copyright (c) 2013 Panayiotis Lipiridis, MIT License.
The SVG files are bundled unchanged except for size optimisation (SVGO) and explicit width and height attributes.


Geo Guess libraries and data
----------------------------
web/vendor/pannellum.* (Pannellum 2.5.6, Matthew Petroff, MIT License, https://pannellum.org) shows the 360 street photos (two small local patches: a picture that finishes loading after its viewer was closed, or a download that failed, is not read again).
web/vendor/leaflet.* (Leaflet 1.9.4, Volodymyr Agafonkin, BSD 2-Clause License, https://leafletjs.com) draws the maps.
Map tiles come from the Esri Canvas Gray basemap (Tiles (c) Esri, DeLorme, NAVTEQ; data (c) OpenStreetMap contributors, ODbL),
with OpenStreetMap standard tiles (https://operations.osmfoundation.org/policies/tiles/) as a fallback. Street photos come from the
Panoramax public instance (https://api.panoramax.xyz), pictures under their authors' open licences (mostly Etalab 2.0, CC-BY,
CC-BY-SA). The game fetches them live and stores nothing; the list of places is web/games/geo/pool.js.


Meta Spotter, Tongue Twister and Invader Hunt data
--------------------------------------------------
web/games/metaspot/data.js: clue notes compiled from geohints.com, plonkit.net and Wikipedia (each entry keeps its source link).
The pictures are simple drawings made in code, not photos.
web/games/tongue/data.js: sample sentences from the Unicode UDHR collection (https://github.com/unicode-org/udhr), language
families and map points from Glottolog (https://glottolog.org, CC-BY 4.0), speaker numbers from the sources linked in each entry.
web/games/invhunt/data.js: Space Invader positions and status from the community dataset by goguelnikov
(https://github.com/goguelnikov/SpaceInvaders, MIT License). The pixel badges are drawn from each ID, not the real artworks.
Map tiles in web/games/tongue/tiles/ and web/games/invhunt/tiles/: (c) OpenStreetMap contributors (ODbL,
https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright), bundled so the games work offline.
